60,3,1,talk,Minako,,We have three options. A is fixed days and a fixed share. B is a booking calendar with costs split by distance. C is a primary keeper.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Option B sounds like the ""auditing"" nightmare I found in the research. Recording every kilometer will just lead to more accusations.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Option A provides the most reliability for my weekly trips, as I'd know exactly which days the car is mine.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shion,,Option A is the most logically sound for the budget. A fixed monthly share eliminates the need to track every single liter of fuel.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Option A sounds the easiest. No booking, no calculating distance, no arguing over who owes what. Just my days and my share.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Minako,,"Option A is simple, but it might be unfair if one person's allotted days are much more valuable than others.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, that's a risk, but Option B's ""distance recording"" is a guaranteed way to sour the group. I prefer the simplicity of A.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Minako, we can rotate the days every few months if the value is uneven. But for now, the certainty of A is what I need.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shion,,"I agree. Option C puts too much burden on one person, and B is too tedious. A is the only one that provides financial clarity without the stress.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,I'm with everyone. Option A means I don't have to spend my weekends doing math. I vote for A.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Minako,,"If the rest of you are so certain, I can see the merit in the peace it brings. It's better than a ""fair"" system that everyone hates.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"It removes the ""favor"" aspect. You don't ask for the car; you simply use it on your day. I vote for A.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Asuka,,It solves the handover anxiety and the scheduling collapses. I vote for A.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shion,,"It's the most efficient way to handle the 280,000 yen and the fuel. I vote for A.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
